BLOCKER (pre-existing, reproduced at HEAD, OUT OF SCOPE — no red-as-green)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  The TeslaSync iOS + macOS app target does NOT compile at the current repo HEAD,
  independent of this unit. Confirmed root cause via the compiler's own candidate
  notes:

    apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/System/StatusApiDocsPage.swift:399
        enum TSSpacing { static let xs/sm/md/lg/xl/... }        ← DUPLICATE
        (and a duplicate `enum TSRadius`)
    apps/design/generated/apple/Tokens.swift:175
        public enum TSSpacing { static let xs/sm/md/lg/... }    ← canonical (P2)

  A second top-level `enum TSSpacing` / `enum TSRadius` declared inside
  StatusApiDocsPage.swift collides with the generated design tokens, so EVERY
  `TSSpacing.*` / `TSRadius.*` reference across the whole module is
  "ambiguous use of 'sm' / 'md' / 'lg' / 'xs' …", which cascades into the
  `#Preview` macro type-check ("ambiguous use of 'Preview'"). Errors are entirely
  in pre-existing files (StatusApiDocsPage, WeekSelector, WeeklyDigest*,
  *.Previews.swift, AIWatchFaceNLResponse*, …); ZERO are in this unit's files.

  PROOF it is not mine: with this unit fully `git stash`-ed (push -u), a clean
  regenerate + `xcodebuild -scheme TeslaSync ... build` at HEAD fails IDENTICALLY
  — HEAD_BUILD_EXIT=65 with the same ambiguous-`TSSpacing` + ambiguous-`Preview`
  errors. So the break exists at HEAD without my changes.

  StatusApiDocsPage.swift lives under Features/System — another page, explicitly
  OUT OF SCOPE for this prompt ("Out of Scope (reject): Other pages") and NOT in
  the Allowed files. It is therefore deliberately NOT modified here.

  ISOLATION PROOF (temporary, reverted, NOT committed): commenting out only the
  two duplicate enums in StatusApiDocsPage.swift and rebuilding drops the iOS
  app-target error count 248 → 49. The 49 that remain are a SEPARATE, also
  pre-existing blocker — an SDK-level "ambiguous use of 'Preview'" (candidate note:
  `UIKit.Preview … found this candidate in module 'UIKit'` vs SwiftUI.Preview) plus
  "ambiguous use of 'accessibilityAddTraits'", in pre-existing files that import
  BOTH UIKit and SwiftUI next to a `#Preview`. That is a toolchain/Xcode-26.5
  condition, not user-fixable from this unit. So a fully green full-app build is
  unreachable in this environment regardless of scope (two independent pre-existing
  blockers). The StatusApiDocsPage edit was reverted via `git checkout` and is NOT
  in the commit. Across ALL THREE failing builds (248 / 49 errors + the test run)
  this unit's files produced ZERO errors — its own `#Preview` blocks are immune to
  the UIKit/SwiftUI ambiguity because the view files import only SwiftUI.

